'''''Colutea orientalis''''' is a species of [[Fabaceae|leguminous]] [[shrub]] native to Europe and Asia. It is a deciduous, grey-leafed, bushy shrub that grows to a height of up to 2&nbsp;m (6&nbsp;ft). It bears clusters of small yellow and coppery-red flowers in summer, followed by green seed pods. ''Colutea'' × ''media'' is a hybrid between ''C. orientalis'' and ''[[Colutea arborescens|C. arborescens]]''.
